From 6b32e2a909a332920625a439d8c969afeb9a842e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RTSP-on-GE11 contributors <noreply@invalid>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 10:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] winedmo: preserve audio timeline across decoder flush

GE's audio decoder used audio_started both to mark the first output sample
and to decide when to establish the output timestamp origin. A Media
Foundation seek flushes the transform and cleared both audio_started and the
established origin. The first decoded AAC sample after a nonzero seek was
therefore rebased from its absolute source timestamp to zero, while the media
session continued comparing samples against the absolute seek position. The
session discarded the entire remaining audio stream as pre-roll and starved
the shared A/V demux path.

Use the timestamp-adjust sentinel together with the existing first-output
guard to decide whether the origin still needs to be established. Preserve
both fields in the established input-to-output timestamp mapping across a
decoder flush. The flush still clears decoder and accumulation state and marks
the first subsequent output as discontinuous. Transform creation and GE's
existing explicit-input-discontinuity path continue to clear the mapping.

The license of the modified Wine source file applies to this patch.

A3.19: rebased after GE-Proton11-6's ge-video-rework set.
---
diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c b/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
index c5111ee11f741efdbbfd44648edae802874e45a2..b4288a7c3f89c2f395ff4c2dc51cf241c9b384ed 100644
--- a/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
@@ -1457,7 +1457,8 @@ NTSTATUS transform_get_output( void *arg )
          * (legacy PROVIDES_SAMPLES query) get STATUS_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL with the full
          * size; all other callers receive up to capacity bytes with INCOMPLETE set when
          * more data remains. */
-        if (!t->audio_started && base_pts != INT64_MIN
+        if (!t->audio_started && t->audio_output_pts_adjust == INT64_MIN
+                && base_pts != INT64_MIN
                 && (t->avctx->codec_id != AV_CODEC_ID_AAC || !t->split_aac_output))
             t->audio_output_pts_adjust = base_pts;
         if (base_pts != INT64_MIN && t->audio_output_pts_adjust != INT64_MIN)
@@ -1598,8 +1599,9 @@ NTSTATUS transform_flush( void *arg )
     t->video_trace_count  = 0;
     t->audio_base_pts     = 0;
     t->last_input_pts     = INT64_MIN;
-    t->audio_pts_offset   = 0;
-    t->audio_output_pts_adjust = INT64_MIN;
+    /* Keep the established input-to-output timestamp mapping across a decoder
+     * flush. Discarding queued decode state does not start a new presentation
+     * timeline; explicit input-discontinuity handling remains separate. */
     t->audio_started      = false;
     t->last_video_pts     = INT64_MIN;
     t->last_video_duration = INT64_MIN;
